+# v34 — recognise dim camera selections
+
+- Fix successful camera selections being rejected because the translucent
+  outline is gray rather than bright white. Detect thin local-contrast lines
+  and the projected camera rectangle instead of imposing a white-pixel cutoff.
+- Require the expected horizontal and vertical geometry where visible so a
+  nearby offset rectangle or a click ripple cannot confirm the wrong target.
+- Recognised selections close the map and inspect the view. Genuinely ignored
+  clicks still retry once and remain unchecked if confirmation fails.
+- Process the rectangle neighbourhood; add no fixed pause, input padding,
+  portal restrictions or changes to map-control boxes and drag bounds.
+- Preserve v33 daily 5/5 collection, 20-second waits, Emerald Corner (241,107)
+  return, 16:00 Europe/Sofia reset, 1h 15s sighting dots, routes, assets,
+  native cursor protection and Gem Spy histories/observation-only behaviour.
+
+Validation includes dim/antialiased outlines on brown/green/snow backgrounds at
+three capture sizes, clipped outlines, offset rectangles, click ripples and
+one-tap/one-Back simulated inspection. The full Windows suite, native UI/input,
+frozen EXE and archive extraction/hash checks are run before publication.
+These checks are not a live BlueStacks game run.
